        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Under aerobic conditions, FeCl2·4H2O (2 mmol, 0.20 g), NaN3 (4 mmol, 0.26 g), and H2mdea (2 mmol, 0.24 g) were combined in MeCN/CH2Cl2 (20 mL, 10:10) with stirring. Hdnbz (1 mmol, 0.21 g) and Y(NO3)3·6H2O (0.5 mmol, 0.093 g) were then added as solids, giving a reddish mixture that was stirred for 1 h and filtered. Slow evaporation of the filtrate in air afforded red crystals in 3 days, which were isolated, washed with MeCN, and dried in air.",
