      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "magnetic",
        "summary": "Diamagnetic Y analogue used as a magnetic reference for the Fe6 core. χMT at room temperature is 23.77 cm3·K·mol−1 (Table 1 lists 24.6), below 26.28–26.3 expected for six uncoupled FeIII (S=5/2, g=2), and falls to 2.56 cm3·K·mol−1 at 1.8 K, indicating dominant antiferromagnetic Fe···Fe coupling. Curie–Weiss fit: C=27.6 cm3·K·mol−1, θ=−49.9 K. Magnetization 10.44 μB at 7 T and 2 K. No SMM or MCE emphasis for 1.",
